          },
          "field": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Field",
            "description": "Grouping parameters only: the stratifier field."
          },
          "fieldType": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Fieldtype",
            "description": "Grouping parameters only: the stratifier's type in the schema."
          },
          "choices": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "additionalProperties": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "type": "object"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Choices",
            "description": "Choice parameters only: the options a UI lists, `{value, label}` each. A `choice` picks how something is computed (a survival estimator)."
          }
        },
        "type": "object",
        "required": [
          "param",
          "placeholder",
          "label",
          "value"
        ],
        "title": "YACVisParam",
        "description": "One re-bindable template parameter, as offered to a UI.\n\nTwo kinds. A ``field`` parameter swaps which column a channel is bound to,\nand its ``value`` is that column's name. A ``grouping`` parameter re-cuts a\nstratifier into named strata, and its ``value`` is the grouping object (or\n``\"\"`` for the ungrouped default) — a client renders it from ``field`` and\n``fieldType``, which say what is being cut and therefore which control fits.\nA ``choice`` picks one of a fixed set of computations, listed in ``choices``."
      }
